<title>ISRAEL: Israeli industrial exports rose 6.7 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Israeli industrial exports rose 6.7 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's industrial exports, not counting polished diamonds, rose 6.7 percent in May from a year earlier to $1.116 billion, the Industry and Trade Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the first five months, industrial exports without diamonds were up 10.2 percent from a year earlier to $5.579 billion, the ministry said.</p>
<p>It said the rise during the January-May period was led by communications, medical and scientific equipment, while textile and clothing exports declined 4.6 percent and food exports by 14.8 percent.</p>
<p>The ministry said that in May alone textile exports showed a slight improvement after a long period of decline.</p>
<p>On a seasonally adjusted basis, it said, industrial exports rose an annualised 15 percent in the March-May period.</p>
<p>-- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502</p>
</text>
